From c4400d849ab8e1b49a76f97a5b084f5aab527499 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 01:37:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 017/104] Unified: a smoother first sketch

- Sketch without a picked face: instead of the full attachment editor,
  the integrated environment asks for one click on a plane or flat face
  and opens the sketch right away (no OK, no attachment modes). The
  origin planes are shown four times larger while choosing.
- Escape only cancels the current sketch tool; the sketch is closed with
  its OK button (default of LeaveSketchWithEscape in single workbench
  mode; a user setting is kept).
- After closing a sketch that no feature uses yet, the context bar offers
  extrude / revolve / edit (and cut in, once the part has a solid) in the
  middle of the view.
- Context bar: a sketch picked anywhere (edges or its inner face) gets the
  sketch actions; command states are tested on the spot, since the
  periodic update may not have run yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
